  "question": {
    "text": "If equal volumes of \\(\\mathrm{AB}_2\\) and XY (both are salts) aqueous solutions are mixed, which of the following combination will give a precipitate of \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) at 300 K ?<br />(Given \\(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) (at 300 K) for \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2=5.2 \\times 10^{-7}\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wpn48",
      "text": "\\(3.6 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{AB}_2, 5.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{XY}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VOOsj",
      "text": "\\(2.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{AB}_2, 0.8 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{XY}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nr7h2",
      "text": "\\(2.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{AB}_2, 2.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{XY}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EHnla",
      "text": "\\(1.5 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{AB}_2, 1.5 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}~ \\mathrm{XY}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When equal volumes are mixed molarity reduce to half.<br />For precipitation \\(\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{SP}}=\\left[\\mathrm{A}^{+2}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{Y}^{-}\\right]^2  \\gt  \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{SP}}\\)<br />(1) \\(\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{SP}}=\\left(1.8 \\times 10^{-3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5}{2} \\times 10^{-4}\\right)^2  \\lt \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sP}}\\)<br />(2) \\(\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{SP}}=\\left(10^{-4}\\right)\\left(0.4 \\times 10^{-3}\\right)^2 \\lt \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\)<br />(3) \\(\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{SP}}=\\left(10^{-2}\\right)\\left(10^{-2}\\right)^2  \\gt  \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sP}}\\)<br />(4) \\(\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{SP}}=\\left(\\frac{1.5}{2} \\times 10^{-4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1.5}{2} \\times 10^{-3}\\right)^2 \\lt \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sP}}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
